WEBVTT

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:06.940
Let's eat.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:11.090
Nya-tan, could you get the soy sauce?

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:13.150
Here you go.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.930
That's sesame oil...

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:19.020
Oops, wrong one. Sorry!

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.950
It's okay. I'll get it.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.960
<b>Soy Sauce</b>

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.960
<b>Sesame Oil</b>

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:32.940
Uri-tan...

00:00:52.010 --> 00:00:54.440
Takeru is sad.

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:57.740
Thanks for the meal.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.390
I'm heading out.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:02.700
Take care!

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:12.910
Takeru!

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:15.260
Nya-tan?

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:17.990
I was taking a walk nearby, 
so I came to meet you!

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:19.320
Oh, and...

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.940
You forgot this.

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.510
Oh, thanks...

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:26.070
What's this?

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:28.620
I'll open that!

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:28.390
Wai—

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:30.210
Hey!

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:35.900
That scared me! It flew everywhere!

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.780
What is this stuff?!

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:37.780
Jeez...

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:40.510
Nobody warned me about this!

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.040
Takeru, you finally laughed.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.690
<b>ETOTAMA</b>

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.270
<b>Eyes of a Rabbit, Ears of a Rabbit</b>

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:38.970
Sorry for the wait.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.590
Thank you very much.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.300
Thanks.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.630
I'll bring your cake right now.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:48.410
Thank you for waiting.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:50.620
Here's the cake you ordered, yep, yep.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.000
"Yep, yep"?

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:02.200
That's hot!

00:04:00.730 --> 00:04:02.640
Wait! Uri-tan, you're alive!

00:04:02.200 --> 00:04:04.330
Wait, no it's not! It's lukewarm!

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.430
For real?! I don't believe it!

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:05.430
You did that on pur—

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.930
<b>We're opening at 
11:00 today!</b>

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.930
<b>Closed for the Day  
Please come again.</b>

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.270
So...

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:13.640
What on Earth is this all about?

00:04:14.140 --> 00:04:15.520
What do you mean?

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:18.770
Yes! This isn't so bad at all!

00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:21.400
You turned into light and died!

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:23.150
Was your defeat by Chu-tan a lie?!

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:24.690
It wasn't a lie.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:26.540
It's true that I died.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.540
But she was reincarnated.

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:29.740
Reincarnated?

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.490
Yes. Even if we die,

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:35.670
we reincarnate after a 
certain amount of time.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:37.150
What kind of system is that?

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:39.210
Exactly that kind of system, apparently.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:42.890
"Apparently"? Did you forget 
that too, Nya-tan?

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.200
Stupid cat...

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.960
Uri-tan, you reincarnated 
three days ago, right?

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.640
You didn't go straight 
to Takeru-san's house?

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:53.360
I got a lecture from the

00:04:53.360 --> 00:04:57.360
ETM12 Executive Committee about 
intervening in a battle first.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:01.090
I'm sorry I worried you, Takeru-san.

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:03.450
W-Well, as long as you're alive...

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:04.650
But you!

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:07.250
If you knew, you should've 
told me, Nya-tan!

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:09.270
I only found out yesterday myself.

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:10.830
I just forgot to tell you.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:14.140
Th-Then is that why you 
were nicer than usual today

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:15.750
and kept trying to cheer me up?

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:19.510
Oh! Nya-tan, give your kindness to me, too!

00:05:19.510 --> 00:05:22.170
Good thing I tied that pervert up first.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:26.490
So Nya-tan was a soothing type 
of character while I was gone?

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:27.340
Was I?

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.300
I... guess so...

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.070
I refuse!

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:30.950
Why?!

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:31.390
<b>Yandere 
Tsundere
Little Sister Character
Little Devil Type
Soothing Type
Herbivore Type
Carnivore Type
Passionate
Laid-back Character
Moe Character</b>

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:34.050
I don't need a character that can 
be explained in words anymore!

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:39.080
I want to have an original character beyond

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.480
anyone's comprehension, 
that's the first of its kind in the world!

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.570
Oh! Amazing!

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.190
You can't just become something original.

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:49.700
That's not true!

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:51.710
I'm a genius,

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:55.040
so I'm gonna produce a picture-perfect 
flawless new me all by myself!

00:05:56.550 --> 00:05:57.860
What did you say?

00:05:57.860 --> 00:05:58.420
Meow?

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.650
An amateur should not

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:03.210
<b>Menacing</b>

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:03.210
speak of production so lightly.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:06.800
Lost children do not realize they are lost!

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:07.770
What?!

00:06:07.770 --> 00:06:11.100
You're right. Nya-tan is lost on 
her journey of self-discovery.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:11.680
That's depressing!

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:16.060
A character that cannot be explained 
might as well not exist!

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:16.930
Shock!

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.040
With such an unstable character,

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.100
even if you join the zodiac, 
no one will remember you.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.440
You'll be forgotten right away.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:23.320
Are you serious?!

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:24.910
No way...

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.610
They won't remember me...

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.200
<b>Did you know the cat has joined the Chinese zodiac?</b>

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:33.200
<i>What? A cat?</i>

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:34.450
<i>No idea!</i>

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.320
Th-This is awful!

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:39.410
If that happens, 
I'll never gather any Sol/Lull!

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:40.490
That's awful, all right.

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:41.270
Sure is.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:44.460
You two shouldn't talk as 
if it doesn't concern you.

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:53.510
<b>Episode 1</b>

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:48.260
Just remember what happened in episode one.

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:50.110
Even though you're part 
of the Chinese zodiac,

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:53.510
<b>Losers</b>

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:53.190
the reality is that people 
don't remember you!

00:06:53.770 --> 00:06:54.850
That's true!

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:55.950
She's right!

00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:58.270
No one remembers us, either!

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:02.060
That must mean none of your 
characters stand out.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:02.930
Depressing!

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:05.330
For 2,000 years now, I've always thought that

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:08.280
all of you were lacking in self-production!

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.760
First of all, you two!

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:10.700
Y-Yes?!

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:11.970
Your characters overlap!

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:12.530
Huh?!

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.030
And you...

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:14.870
Y-Yeah?

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:15.860
...fall flat off the starting line!

00:07:16.780 --> 00:07:17.800
You...

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:20.500
You've settled into the exposition 
character role too much!

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:22.370
And finally...

00:07:22.670 --> 00:07:23.520
Nya-tan!

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:24.130
What?!

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:28.150
The mutability of your character 
is simply beyond my tolerance!

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:28.880
For real?!

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:32.380
Oh, no! Takeru, we're having an emergency 
character-planning meeting tonight!

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:36.640
Panic Panic

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.850
That's not something you just say like 
"We're having sukiyaki tonight."

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:37.640
Sukiyaki?!

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:40.730
Ah, that was the best kicking 
and stomping I've ever had.

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:43.400
<i>Your</i> character never fails.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:45.690
Good work, everyone!

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:48.230
I'm hungry! Let's hurry 
home and have sukiyaki!

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:52.360
La, la, la! La, la, la! Sukiyaki!

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.360
This character-planning meeting 
is totally sukiyaki now.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:56.740
While we eat sukiyaki, we'll have 
an "Uri-tan's Back" party, too!

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:03.860
Our characters don't stand out.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:06.460
We're lacking self-production.

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:08.670
Our characters overlap.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:12.470
If you've thought that for 2,000 years, 
you should've told us sooner!

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:16.220
But being told straight-up 
like that stings, huh?

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:21.350
Didn't Nya-tan say she's having a
 character-planning meeting at Takeru's tonight?

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:23.350
Oh... Yeah.

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:29.070
That must mean none of your 
characters stand out.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:30.470
And you...

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:31.360
Y-Yeah?

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:32.280
...fall flat off the starting line!

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.450
I can't get their words out of my head.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:45.750
Now that I've said that to all of them,

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.720
I just can't let this go.

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:49.710
Inabaman No. 1, change of plans.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:52.670
We're going to Takeru's house.

00:08:52.670 --> 00:08:53.220
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:56.210 --> 00:08:58.070
Hello, No. 55?

00:08:58.440 --> 00:08:59.970
Yes, it's me.

00:08:59.970 --> 00:09:02.240
Prepare the usual right away.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:06.990
Shopping!

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:07.530
Meat!

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:08.690
Shopping!

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:09.570
Meat!

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.480
<b>Sukiyaki</b>

00:09:10.870 --> 00:09:12.800
Looks tasty!

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:14.600
Free samples here!

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:15.780
Meow! What?!

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:20.120
Nya-tan

00:09:22.160 --> 00:09:24.960
Thank you for
 your purchase!

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:24.400
Sukiyaki time!

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:26.010
Yo.

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:27.330
We're here.

00:09:27.550 --> 00:09:28.910
How'd you get in here?

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:29.800
There.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:31.090
<b>Hole</b>

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.050
And I thought I'd subtly covered that...

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.510
He was subtly denying us!

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.710
After being subjected to 
our whims all this time,

00:09:36.710 --> 00:09:39.800
I thought he was grudgingly 
starting to accept us...

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.560
He's still a tough nut to crack.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:43.330
You're here, too, Piyo-tan?

00:09:43.330 --> 00:09:45.670
Hey, you guys, what was—

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:46.310
Ow!

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:47.810
<b>One Step</b>

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:48.560
<b>Two Steps  One Step</b>

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:49.100
<b>Three Steps  Two Steps  One Step</b>

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.710
Looks like she forgot again.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:58.730
She really did fall flat right 
off the starting line.

00:09:58.730 --> 00:10:01.370
But maybe the fact that she 
can use it over and over

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.880
means her character does stand 
out, in its own way...

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:06.370
What's going on?!

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:08.050
Hey, look!

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.250
It's the UTC,

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.880
Usa-tan Company's helicopter!

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:15.130
Usa-tan Company?

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:32.060
Wh-What was that 
Hollywood entrance for?

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.920
Perhaps I wanted you to directly experience

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:38.650
the scope of my ability as a producer!

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:44.030
<b>[Zodiac Precepts ~Article 1: The Divine Ritual] 
The Eto-shin Selection Festival (ETM12) is a divine ritual
 in which an Eto-musume invokes her right to issue
 an inescapable challenge to an Eto-shin, 
